  "name": "VFM_09_Legs",
  "lookup_name": "VFM_09_Legs",
  "description": "Vector & Forces Museum, hall 9 - Legs. Seven walkers in one row, one leg to eight, with every other thing about them held equal: the same scale, the same pace, the same short leash. One leg can only pogo. Two fall and catch. Three stand without negotiating with falling. Four pair diagonally. Five cannot mirror a gait and have to invent one. Six run two alternating tripods. Eight is the crawler with its hunt switched off. They stand on the floor rather than on plinths because they walk. Teleporter south-east to the Arena, where the four-leg rung's descendant is still walking.",
